Z||000000||jasonl||02-02-2001||12:31 PM||||Still having trouble trying to get my 88' 2.8 to pass emissions.  The high reading I am getting is from carbon monoxide and i am not sure(unless the catalytic converter is bad) what it could be.  Fixed all egr problems that I know of, and I'm not getting any engine lights(anymore).  Is there any other ways of testing the cat converter other than checking for loose ceramic?  Any help is appreciated.||||reg||5
Z||000001||stsmithgt||02-02-2001||05:24 PM||||Did they check your timing before doing the smog test.  Mine was a little too far advanced and it sent my emissions way up the scale to fail.  They set the timing and I passed emissions by having readings at about half of what was required.  I had a bad CAT before and it rattled like a MOE FOE.  If there was loose ceramic, I think you would here it. Good luck. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||daved||02-02-2001||06:21 PM||||I think you are running too rich.<P>"Carbon monoxide is formed whenever carbon or substances containing carbon are burned with an insufficient air supply" <P>Probably your oxygen sensor is getting past its best, or your plugs are weak. <P> You did do a tune-up before you took it in?<P>My V6 passed with flying colours: new o2 sensor and plugs, but original cat!  Hope this helps a bit||||reg||1
